      <PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>The Brain Observatory is a nonprofit organization advancing the study of the human brain and public understanding of neuroscience. It conducts research in brain imaging and neurodegenerative disease and offers hands-on education programs for students teachers and the community. Its mission is to make neuroscience accessible through real laboratory experiences and the preservation of human brain data for research and learning.</PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>The Brain Observatory provides neuroscience-based STEM programs for students and teachers across San Diego County. Activities include afterschool and in-school enrichment field trips to the downtown laboratory seasonal camps research internships and teacher professional development. During the year the organization served more than 3,000 students and educators through hands-on learning with real laboratory materials and data. The nonprofit also generates program income by providing its science curriculum and instructional services to public school districts and community partners. These programs support workforce readiness in life sciences and increase access to quality STEM education for underrepresented youth.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>98445</GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>
        <ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>80000</ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>Public Engagement and Community Outreach: The Brain Observatory maintains a science gallery in downtown San Diego that welcomes visitors to learn about brain science through exhibitions guided tours and community events. Programs such as public open houses workshops and special exhibitions provide hands-on access to real research environments and materials. In 2024 more than 2,000 visitors participated in public events workshops and demonstrations. These activities promote community awareness of neuroscience and strengthen connections between scientific research and public education.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>11000</GrantsAndAllocationsAmt>
        <ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>32818</ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>Neuroscience Research and Brain Imaging: The Brain Observatory participates in collaborative research in brain imaging and neurodegenerative disease. These collaborations with universities and clinicians aim to identify structural biomarkers across imaging and histological modalities. Currently this research is funded in part by income generated through the organizations STEM education and individual contributions.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
